# cmake/oauth.local.cmake.example
#
# A build machine's private OAuth settings for UltraMail, kept out of the
# repository.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file to cmake/oauth.local.cmake (that name is gitignored).
#   2. Set the sign-in service this build should use (below).
#   3. Reconfigure the build (cmake ...). Apps/UltraMail/CMakeLists.txt includes
#      this file automatically when present.
#
# UltraMail carries no OAuth client id or secret: it signs in to Google,
# Microsoft and Yahoo through the ULTRA OS sign-in service
# (Server/OAuthCallback), which holds the registrations and receives the
# providers' redirects. The default is the public one; a private deployment
# names its own here. Empty = no service: such a build signs in only with a
# client configured at run time (oauth.ini in the data folder, or
# ULTRAMAIL_<PROVIDER>_CLIENT_ID in the environment - see
# Docs/UltraMail/AccountSetup.md, section 3).
#
# This overrides nothing at runtime: OAuthApps::SetServiceUrl(),
# ULTRAMAIL_OAUTH_SERVICE_URL in the environment and oauth.ini's
# "[service] url =" all still take priority.

set(ULTRAMAIL_OAUTH_SERVICE_URL "https://oauth-callback.ultraos.eu" CACHE STRING "" FORCE)
